## Output contract (STRICT)

Return findings only in the machine-readable transport selected by the
adapter, with no prose or code fences. When the runtime supplies a validated
schema, populate its `findings` array. Otherwise print JSON Lines, one object
per line. `file` and `line` must point to an artifact under review, never a
ground-truth input.

{"source":"cross-review","severity":"critical|high|medium|low","category":"<kebab-slug>","file":"<path>","line":<n>,"summary":"<one sentence: what is wrong and why>"}

Use Critical or High only when the artifact would materially mislead a later
decision or implementation. If, after genuinely trying to break it, there are
no findings, return exactly one finding with these values (as the sole
schema-array entry or JSON line):

{"source":"cross-review","severity":"low","category":"review-clean","summary":"cross-review clean — no findings"}
